.TH THURVTLD 8 "" "Thur VTL" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
thurvtld \- Thur VTL daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B thurvtld
[\fB\-c\fR \fIPATH\fR | \fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-test\fR]
[\fB\-\-help\fR]
[\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B thurvtld
is the Thur VTL daemon: a spec-conformant SMC-3 medium changer plus
SSC-4 LTO drive emulation exposed as an iSCSI target. Cartridge data
is content-addressed and deduplicated, with chunks tiered out to S3,
GCS, Azure, or a local filesystem.

The daemon owns one library / chassis instance (initialized once via
.BR thurvtl (1)
.BR "library init" ),
listens for iSCSI sessions on the configured port (3260 by default),
serves the admin Unix socket at
.I /run/thurvtl/admin.sock
for the CLI, and exposes Prometheus metrics + health endpoints on
the HTTP listener (9090 by default).

It is not started automatically by the package postinst \(em the
operator edits the conffile, runs
.BR "thurvtl library init" ,
then
.BR "systemctl enable --now thurvtld" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR \fIPATH\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR=\fIPATH\fR
Path to the YAML configuration file. Defaults to
.IR /etc/thurvtl/thurvtl.yaml .
.TP
\fB\-\-test\fR
Run an in-process smoke test (cartridge / library / S3 / prefetch /
\(cqstop) and exit. Does not start the daemon, does not bind ports.
Useful for packaging CI.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print short usage and exit.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version (crate version plus the git SHA the binary was built
from) and exit.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGTERM
Graceful shutdown: drain in-flight SCSI commands, flush dirty chunks
to the configured pool, release the admin socket, exit zero.
.TP
.B SIGINT
Same as
.BR SIGTERM .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/thurvtl/thurvtl.yaml
Daemon configuration (mode 0640, root:thurvtl). Minimal starter
shipped at install. The
.B full annotated reference for every key
is at
.IR /usr/share/doc/thurvtl/thurvtl.defaults.yaml ;
.B "thurvtl config defaults"
prints the same content to stdout.
.TP
.I /etc/thurvtl/thurvtl.env
Optional daemon environment file (cloud credentials,
.RI ${ ENV_VAR }
references from thurvtl.yaml). 0640 root:thurvtl. Read by
.B thurvtld.service
via
.BR EnvironmentFile= .
.TP
.I /var/lib/thurvtl/
Default data directory: library + inventory (\fIlibrary/\fR),
cartridge manifests (\fItapes/\fR), the local chunk pool
(\fIchunks/\fR), and the audit log (\fIaudit/\fR). Overridable via
.B data_dir
in the conffile.
.TP
.I /run/thurvtl/admin.sock
Admin Unix socket (mode 0660, peer-cred authed). CLI commands that
require a live daemon route through it; the
.B thurvtl
group has connect access.
.TP
.I /var/lib/thurvtl/.daemon.lock
PID lockfile. CLI mutating commands refuse if a daemon is alive on
the same data directory. Stale locks auto-clear.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Standard
.BR tracing-subscriber
filter directive (e.g.
.BR RUST_LOG=info,thurvtl=debug ).
Defaults to
.B info
when unset. Read at startup; restart the daemon to apply a change.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR thurvtl (1),
.BR systemctl (1)

The shipped reference YAML at
.I /usr/share/doc/thurvtl/thurvtl.defaults.yaml
documents every configuration key.
